<http://localhost:5002/osn-doi-10-26249-fk2-dmdlte> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/osn-doi-10-26249-fk2-dmdlte> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.26249%2FFK2%2FDMDLTE>.
<http://localhost:5002/osn-doi-10-26249-fk2-dmdlte> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Ada 2025: a multimodal dataset for water-deficit stress detection in sugar beets".
<http://localhost:5002/osn-doi-10-26249-fk2-dmdlte> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A comprehensive multimodal dataset of greenhouse-grown sugar beets. Data was collected automatically between August 12, 2025 and September 22, 2025. The dataset follows the plants from seeding to a predetermined growth stage and contains hyperspectral, thermal, RGB, and depth imagery of the plants during this period, with dry stress induced in 2/3 of the plants on September 3, 2025. Environmental data and metadata are also provided. The data subcollections for each modality can be accessed at the links below.  <br> <br> Note that the current version of the public dataset temporarily contains only the data relevant to review of the associated conference paper, with a subsequent full dataset release pending publication.<br> <br> Hyperspectral Data - <a href=\\'https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/PK9YDR\\'>https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/PK9YDR</a><br>  Thermal Data - <a href=\\'https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/ASL0BV\\'>https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/ASL0BV</a><br>  RGB Data - <a href=\\'https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/FGLG94\\'>https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/FGLG94</a><br>  Depth Data - <a href=\\'https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/SMHP1Y\\'>https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/SMHP1Y</a><br>  Environmental & Metadata - <a href=\\'https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/C0HOBN\\'>https://doi.org/10.26249/FK2/C0HOBN</a>  <br> <br> This work was supported by the Lower Saxony Ministry of Science and Culture (MWK), funded through the zukunft.niedersachsen program of the Volkswagen Foundation, as part of two projects (ZN4219 - HybrInt and ZN4661 - RLA). We also thank the agrifood-TEF-DE project for additional hardware support.".
